# =============================================================================
# Smart Construction Connect — FRONTEND environment
# =============================================================================
#
# In production, this frontend talks to the backend through the rewrites in
# vercel.json (which proxy /api, /uploads and /company_data to your Render
# backend). So NO environment variable is strictly required on Vercel.
#
# In local development, `vite.config.ts` already proxies /api, /uploads and
# /company_data to http://localhost:8000, so no .env is needed either — just
# run the backend on :8000 and `npm run dev` here.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the client bundle.
#
# VITE_API_URL — your Render backend's public origin, e.g.
#   https://smart-construction-connect-api.onrender.com
# REQUIRED on Vercel for real-time messaging: Vercel's rewrites proxy HTTP but
# NOT WebSockets, so the chat socket connects to the backend directly using this.
# Leave it UNSET for local dev (the Vite dev server proxies the socket).
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com

# Example:
# VITE_APP_NAME=Smart Construction Connect
